---
title: Thai red curry with chicken
servings: 4
tags: [chicken, gluten-free]
cuisine: thai
time: 45 minutes
source: Authentic Thai Red Curry with Chicken by Pailin Chongchitnant, Hot Thai Kitchen, https://hot-thai-kitchen.com/red-curry-chicken-squash
---

== Curry ==

Scrub the @kabocha squash{2%cups}, trim any blemished skin, scoop out the seeds and cut into bite-sized cubes.

Boil the @coconut milk{1 1/2%cup} and stir in the @red curry paste{3 1/2-5%tbsp}. Reduce over medium-high heat until very thick and the oil separates.

Toss in the @chicken thigh{1%lb}. Add the @chicken stock{1%cup}, @fish sauce{2%tbsp} and @palm sugar{2-3%tbsp} and simmer ~{8%minutes}.

Add the squash and simmer ~{6-8%minutes}, until a fork goes in easily but it holds its shape.

Off the heat, season with more @fish sauce{}; curry pastes vary in salt. Stir in the @Thai basil leaves{1%cup} and @?red bell pepper{1/4}(julienned).

Serve at once with jasmine rice.

== Red curry paste (optional) ==

Seed the @?mild dried chilies{0.4%oz} and cut into chunks, then grind fine in a spice grinder.

In a heavy #mortar and pestle{}, pound the @?lemongrass{3%tbsp}(finely chopped), @?galangal{1%tbsp}(finely chopped), @?cilantro roots{2}(chopped), @?makrut lime zest{1%tsp}, @?white peppercorns{1/4%tsp} and @?salt{1%tsp} until fine.

Pound in the ground chilies, then the @?garlic{3%tbsp}(chopped) and @?shallots{1/4%cup}(chopped) until fine. Pound in the @?fermented shrimp paste{1%tsp}.
